ron: Charlotte Osgood Mason, a wealthy white woman who insisted on being called 'Godmother.' Paying them lavishly while trying to control their work, Mason may have been the spark for their bitter falling-out. Was the split inevitable when Hughes decided to be financially independent of their patron? Was Hurston jealous of the woman employed as their typist? Or was the rupture over the authorship of Mule Bone?","publicationYear":2019,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Hurston, zora neale, 1901-1960","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-zora-and-langston-yuval-taylor"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Hughes, langston, 1902-1967","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-zora-and-langston-yuval-taylor"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"African american authors","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-zora-and-langston-yuval-taylor"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Authors, biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-zora-and-langston-yuval-taylor"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"New York Times reviewed","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-zora-and-langston-yuval-taylor"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-zora-and-langston-yuval-taylor"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"BIOGRAPHY & AUTOBIOGRAPHY / Literary Figures","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-zora-and-langston-yuval-taylor"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"BIOGRAPHY & AUTOBIOGRAPHY / Cultural, Ethnic & Regional / African American & Black","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-zora-and-langston-yuval-taylor"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"African American women authors","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-zora-and-langston-